## 4. The "do it by Thursday" tier — 90-day pilots under $100K each

1. **Concourse E gate-local announcement pilot (before opening).** Reconfigure PA zoning so that only TSA, mass notification, and irregular-ops announcements go terminal-wide; airline boarding audio is confined to a 50-foot radius. Measure: announcement count/hour, adjacent-zone spillover in dB(A), STI at each seat cluster, and missed-boarding delta versus a matched non-pilot concourse. Cost: \$30K in commissioning and acoustic-testing fees. Time: 45 days from Design Manual directive. Evidence produced: whether the SFO result transfers to a Saarinen-adjacent, United-dominant hub geometry.
2. **FIDS-audio silent boarding at five IAD gates.** At five volunteer United gates, install per-monitor audio amplification (roughly \$200 in parts per monitor: small Class-D amp, PoE-powered, hidden behind the panel). Every boarding-status change on the FIDS triggers a short chime + text-to-speech announcement heard only in the immediate seating area. Kill the mic-on-podium announcement entirely for those five gates for 30 days. Measure missed-boarding rate, passenger satisfaction (intercept survey), and gate-agent workload. Cost: \$15K including a customer-experience contractor to run the intercept surveys. Evidence produced: whether Solution D's premise — that people follow the visual channel if the audio is co-located — actually holds at a US hub.
3. **Pop-up quiet room at IAD Main Terminal mezzanine or Concourse B under-utilized area.** 30-day pop-up. Repurpose ~800 sq ft. Portable acoustic panels, dimmable lighting rental, contract customer-experience host (32 hours/day across two shifts), Sunflower Lanyard supply. Log occupancy, dwell time, and post-visit survey. Cost: \$50K for the 30-day pop-up including staffing. Evidence produced: whether the demand exists to justify a permanent Concourse E pod, and what geographic distribution (landside vs. airside, near-gate vs. central) drives use.

Three pilots. All three finished before Concourse E opens in September 2026. Combined budget under \$100K. Combined evidence base sufficient to defend or kill the full standard at the FY2027 capital-planning cycle.

